<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: Are Germans giving up their beloved meat and sausages?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5410512810c810934691fb1d6da644ba1c64e70c38ac6ae5b9166d58432ae81</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-are-germans-giving-up-their-beloved-meat-and-sausages/live-79441034--d9fb5f1aa888.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-are-germans-giving-up-their-beloved-meat-and-sausages/live-79441034?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germans used to be all about sausages and meat. While those do remain popular, things seem to be slowly changing. There also are new insights into the economic side of East Germany's espionage DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Two people killed as bus crashes on way to Oktoberfest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d2f97392a31e7b258db78d4e9bf3cf3d05e436fa2e7bdad27e77a56d7633cf7</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T15:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-people-killed-as-bus-crashes-on-way-to-oktoberfest/a-79450016--d10b8bca83ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-people-killed-as-bus-crashes-on-way-to-oktoberfest/a-79450016?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bus was traveling from Italy to Munich, carrying 33 Filipino tourists who wanted to visit the famous beer festival. One of the dozens injured remains in life-threatening condition.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German Olympic Committee names Munich as bid city choice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58289cffa90f071006e53e552614537228fd7d2f44233fe217ecd44afc0e2cd1</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-olympic-committee-names-munich-as-bid-city-choice/a-79441284--424a4614f81d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-olympic-committee-names-munich-as-bid-city-choice/a-79441284?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich has been voted as the city that will bid for the Olympics in 2036, 2040 or 2044. Berlin had been in the running but withdrew on Thursday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD, CDU ban new Holocaust 'stumbling stones' in Heidenau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:153e3b37150fd35aeaa7a642d751f99a65361fd242a99f21ee620a9ac3371a87</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-cdu-ban-new-holocaust-stumbling-stones-in-heidenau/a-79433919--bafd061ca07a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-cdu-ban-new-holocaust-stumbling-stones-in-heidenau/a-79433919?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Activists, politicians and representatives of Holocaust victims reacted with anger after the center-right CDU party joined forces with the AfD to ban new Stolpersteine (stumbling stones) in the eastern town of Heidenau.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bundesliga, other top European leagues call for major FIFA reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffe4fd89fab3f8599c026406abfec4875d1753b020ecd19d4ca47b5ed6de40d2</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:40Z